# E-1153: For $x_1,\ldots,x_n\in [-1,1]$ let\[l_k(x)=\frac{\prod_{i\neq k}(x-x_i)}{\prod_{i\neq k}(x_k-x_i)},\]which are such that $l_k(x_k)=1$ and $l_k(x_i)=0$ for $i\neq k$. Let\[\lambda(x)=\sum_k \lvert l_k(x)\rvert.\]Is it true that, for any fixed $-1\leq a< b\leq 1$,\[\max_{x\in [a,b]}\lambda(x)> \left(\frac{2}{\pi}-o(1)\right)\log n?\]
